## Why This Is Asked

Tests concrete application of 3-valued logic to pipeline gating, not just theory. Requires constructing a satisfiable partial assignment and a propagation strategy that avoids prematurely forcing F.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene three-valued logic: T>U>F ordering; ¬, ∧, ∨, → semantics
- Backtracking/forward-chaining under partial info
- Satisfiability with Unknowns in real-world policy constraints

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple Kleene-like 3-valued evaluator for our constraints
const V = {T:2, U:1, F:0};
function not(x){ return x===V.T?V.F : x===V.F?V.T : V.U; }
function or(a,b){ return a>b? a:b; }
function and(a,b){ return a<b? a:b; }
function imp(a,b){ // a -> b is (!a) OR b
  return or(not(a), b);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend to detect unsat under extra constraints? 
- How does the choice of truth ordering affect propagation?

